findings.body:
The PR deletes `const router = useRouter()` and the `useRouter` import from `BookerWebWrapper.tsx`, but the component still calls `router.push(...)` in several places. This is a TypeScript error (`Cannot find name 'router'`) and a runtime ReferenceError as soon as the booker navigates, which affects every public booking page and embed that renders this wrapper.

::code{file="apps/web/modules/bookings/components/BookerWebWrapper.tsx" lines="190-196"}

::callout{type="warning"}
Grep at the head commit shows `router.push` at lines 193, 228, 232 and 238, with no `const router` or `useRouter` left in the file. The removal looks like an over-eager cleanup of an unused-looking binding.

::

When moving `sortHosts` into `hostGroupUtils.ts`, the equal-weight branch changed from `priorityB - priorityA` to `priorityA - priorityB`. The non-weighted branch still uses `priorityB - priorityA`, so the two modes now disagree. This changes the order of hosts in the round-robin priority list for the `isRRWeightsEnabled` case, where weights tie. The comparator is used by `HostEditDialogs`, `EventTeamAssignmentTab` and `useEventTypeForm`, so the change reaches all three UI paths.

::diff{file="packages/lib/bookings/hostGroupUtils.ts" lines="50-54"}

No test exercises `sortHosts`, so this regression would not be caught by CI. The PR description asks reviewers to verify this move, and this is the specific thing that changed.

::suggestion{file="packages/lib/bookings/hostGroupUtils.ts" lines="51-53"}
    if (weightA === weightB) {
      return priorityB - priorityA;
    } else {
      return weightB - weightA;
    }
